WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.000
 

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:04.000
 

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:04.600
 

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:07.240
We hear so many sounds in our surrounding in our daily life.

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:08.140
 

00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:10.700
When a lion roars we hear a sound.

00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:11.200
 

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:16.280
If we pluck the string of a musical instrument, say a guitar, we hear a sound.

00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:16.840
 

00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:18.520
Water pouring into a glass,

00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:19.020
 

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:20.060
bat hitting the ball,

00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:20.560
 

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:22.740
water hitting the rocks, etc,

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:23.240
 

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:25.160
are some of the examples of different sounds.

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:25.660
 

00:00:25.660 --> 00:00:28.280
Sound plays a very inportant role in our life.

00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:28.780
 

00:00:28.780 --> 00:00:29.740
And most importantly,

00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:30.240
 

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:32.840
it helps us to communicate with each other.

00:00:33.020 --> 00:00:36.900
Have you ever thought about what actually produces the sound?

00:00:37.460 --> 00:00:41.780
To answer this question first we need to understand vibration.

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:44.020
What is vibration?

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:48.100
It is "To and Fro" or "Back and Forth" motion of an object.

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:51.700
For example, if we stratch this rubber band with one hand

00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:52.980
and pluck it in the middle,

00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:55.280
it starts to move back and forth.

00:00:55.960 --> 00:00:58.180
In short, it starts to vibrate.

00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:02.320
It is that vibration, that produces the sound.

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:05.920
Yes, anything that vibrates will produce sound.

00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:09.360
We will learn more about this in the next video

00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:12.780
We know that the voice of adults and children differ.

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:15.800
Why is that that the sounds are different?

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:18.140
What separates the sounds?

00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:21.000
Why is it that some sounds are louder than the others?

00:01:21.740 --> 00:01:25.300
Why are some of the sounds pleasant while other ones are annoying?

00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:29.340
We will answer all these questions in the coming videos

00:01:29.960 --> 00:01:32.775
these are the points that we are going to elaborate on

00:01:32.775 --> 00:01:35.795
in this series of videos based on sound

00:01:35.795 --> 00:01:38.385
vibrating bodies produce sound

00:01:38.385 --> 00:01:41.135
medium of propagation of sound

00:01:41.135 --> 00:01:44.065
amplitude ,frequency and Time period of vibration

00:01:44.135 --> 00:01:47.145
Loudness and pitch

00:01:47.145 --> 00:01:50.920
Audible and Inaudible sounds

00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:52.000
